## Common Pitfalls

- Horizon only works with the Redis queue driver. Other drivers such as database and SQS are not supported.
- Redis Cluster is not supported. Horizon requires a standalone Redis connection.
- Always check ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___config/horizon.php___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ before making changes to understand the current supervisor and environment configuration.
- The ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___environments___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ array overrides only the keys you specify. It merges into ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___defaults___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ and does not replace it.
- The timeout chain must be ordered: job ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___timeout___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ less than supervisor ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___timeout___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ less than ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___retry_after___SINGLE_BACKTICK___. The wrong order can cause jobs to be retried before Horizon finishes timing them out.
- The metrics dashboard stays blank until ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___horizon:snapshot___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ is scheduled. Running ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___{{ $assist->artisanCommand('horizon') }}___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ alone does not populate metrics.
- Always use ___SINGLE_BACKTICK___search-docs___SINGLE_BACKTICK___ for the latest Horizon documentation rather than relying on this skill alone.
